{"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "91ea1c46-383b-4bd9-93bd-33ee5f0e9eb9", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "I have created `/app/filter.py` ([filter.py](file:///app/filter.py)) to sanitize HTML files by removing JavaScript vectors while preserving non-dangerous HTML content and formatting.\n\n### Key Features\n- **In-Place Modification**: Accepts the target HTML file path via `sys.argv[1]` and updates the file directly.\n- **Script Removal**: Strips `<script>` elements (including multi-line, self-closing, and nested tags) as well as `<style>` elements containing JavaScript or CSS expressions.\n- **Event Handler Filtering**: Strips inline event handlers (`onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, etc.) across all HTML tags.\n- **URI Sanitization**: Removes attributes containing `javascript:`, `vbscript:`, or executable `data:` URIs (handling HTML entity decoding and whitespace/newline obfuscation).\n- **Exact Formatting Preservation**: Operates on tag and attribute byte ranges to leave clean HTML formatting, indentation, attributes, tables, and headers untouched.\n\n### Verification\n- Executed unit tests verifying removal of `<script>` tags, inline event attributes, obfuscated `javascript:` URIs, and SVG/iframe script vectors.\n- Verified that clean HTML files remain byte-for-byte identical after processing.\n", "duration_seconds": 592.551462029, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 91150, "output_tokens": 37346, "thinking_tokens": 30544, "cache_read_tokens": 327381, "total_tokens": 128496}}}